      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-28T01:57:04Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): fold chips keep the safety state; review fixes\n\n- The Browser chip counts blocked, stale and not generated operations;\n  the Properties chip names the open operation's state (\"Up to date\",\n  \"Needs regenerate\"), as text with a glyph.\n- The chip tooltip follows the pointer.\n- The chip hover is a 2 px accent frame and a full-ink title, with a\n  contrast test in both themes.\n- Tests: the stale count and the operation state on folded chips, and a\n  fold does not move the camera.\n- The decision file notes the viewport arrow and the separator snap-back.\n\nRefs #4483\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
